<p>Use this dialog box to specify the detailed settings for the Designate/Chapter 
 function.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="number" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span></p>
<p>Enter the page number on which a new chapter begins. If you specify 
 the page range, use a hyphen between page numbers. If you enter multiple 
 numbers, use a comma to separate entries.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The Designate/Chapter function is unavailable 
 within the specified range of pages on the specified paper.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="chaptermode" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span></p>
<p>Select one of the print mode options for the pages specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: Leave Blank</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Inserts a blank sheet as a separator from a different 
 tray selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> before the page 
 specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: One Side</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page 
 Number:</span> on a chapter cover from the tray selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Input 
 Tray:</span>. If you enable this setting, sheets will be printed on the 
 front side only, even if you have specified 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: Both Sides</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page 
 Number:</span> on the front side of a chapter cover from a different tray 
 selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> and the next page 
 on the back side. This option is for 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Chapter</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page 
 Number:</span> on the front side of the sheet at all times while in 2 
 sided print mode. With this selection, you will be unable to use a different 
 input tray setting than the other pages.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designated Sheet Print</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the specified range of pages on different 
 sheets of paper.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="chaptertray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select the tray containing the paper to use for the chapter covers.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="chapterpapertype" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray:</span></p>
<p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to use when using bypass 
 tray paper for Designate/Chapter. Available media types differ depending 
 on the printer you are using.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Plain &amp; Recycled (Auto. for Postcard)</span>, it is normally printed as plain paper/recycled paper. If the print paper size is postcard, print with a paper type suitable for postcards.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="add" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Add</span></p>
<p>Click this to add your specifications of <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Mode:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Input 
 Tray:</span> to the <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Settings List:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="modify" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Modify</span></p>
<p>Click this to change a setting in <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Settings List:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="list" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Settings List:</span></p>
<p>Lists the print modes specified for the chapter covers and their corresponding 
 pages.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="delete" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span></p>
<p>Click this to remove an unnecessary item after selecting it in <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Settings List:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="deleteall" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Delete All</span></p>
<p>Click this to delete all the items in <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter 
 Settings List:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
